        body: ['a {colour} sheen on the skin, strongest at the shoulders and down the outside of the arms, where the scales are small and close as a snake\'s. Hair the wrong kind of heavy, always damp. Gill-lines at the throat, three each side, that flutter when {rm_they} laughs; webbing between the fingers to the second knuckle; {eyes} with a second clear lid that slides across. Legs on land and, {rm_they} says, a tail in the lake', 'cool to stand near, {colour} scales at the collarbone, the backs of the hands, the shins, catching the light when {rm_they} moves. Fins, small and translucent, at the forearms and the backs of the calves. Gills closed and dry on land, opening pink when {rm_they} is wet; {eyes}. Feet slightly too long, webbed, that {rm_they} keeps bare', 'long-limbed and {colour} in a certain light, webbing between the fingers, a voice that carries under water and over it. {eyes}, larger than a human\'s, with no white at all. Faint lines at the neck where the gills are. Skin cold as the lake and smelling of it'],
